  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3632 (#3627). Two notes; none can cause a wrong program today.\n\n1. **Cost.** After #3632, `emit_runs` (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/march.rs`) scans all facets for `model_top` at each call. `flow.rs:201` calls it one time for each piece with `continuing` true, so the plain hop does not run and each scan is wasted. On a large mesh with many pieces this costs time. Compute the value only when the first plain hop needs it, or give it in from the caller.\n2. **Shank under an overhang.** `straight_ok` checks the ball only. Facets with all vertices above the ball centre plus the radius are dropped. For a model with an undercut, a move across below the model top does not check the shank. When the height is at or above the model top, the full tool is above the part. State this limit in the provenance comment, or add the shank to the check.\n",
